# Data Cleaner Studio (web) — never commit secrets or user data.

# --- Supabase credentials: NEVER commit. Ever. ---
# supabase_config.json holds the project URL + anon key. The anon key is
# safe to expose by Supabase's design, but the file still stays out of
# git — it identifies the project, and keeping secrets out of the repo
# is the rule, not the exception.
# The SERVICE-ROLE key must NEVER be in a file at all: it lives only in
# the SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY environment variable (server-side).
# If it ever leaks, roll it in the Supabase dashboard (Settings -> API
# -> Generate new keys) immediately.
supabase_config.json

# --- User data (per-user files, local accounts DB, scheduler state) ---
data/

# --- Python ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- Local config / secrets ---
.env
*.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
.test-venv/
